(---) Tj
T*
(Notice: White rice export ban from 5 December) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] The Realm Trade Ministry gives notice that exports of ordinary white rice) Tj
T*
(are prohibited with immediate effect from 5 December 2026.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] The prohibition follows a harvest 14 percent below the previous year and a) Tj
T*
(rise of about 35 percent in domestic rice prices by late November.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] Two categories are exempt. Premium aromatic rice may continue to be) Tj
T*
(exported. Government-to-government contracts signed before 1 October 2026 may) Tj
T*
(also continue.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] The exemption for government-to-government contracts applies only to the) Tj
T*
(volumes and buyers named in those contracts. It does not cover new contracts or) Tj
T*
(spot sales.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] Exporters must declare the category of every shipment at Vanir Rice Port.) Tj
T*
(Shipments that do not meet the exemption rules will not be cleared.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] The ministry will publish detailed exemption rules within three days.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] The notice is the first formal step in the new policy and follows a period) Tj
T*
(of consultation with producers and buyers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P8] Ministry officials will publish further guidance on the exemption process,) Tj
T*
(including the documents exporters must present at the port.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P9] Firms that ship rice should review their forward purchases and prepare the) Tj
T*
(paperwork well before the first cargo is loaded.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P10] Signed: Priya Lund, trade official, Vanir.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
